# .cursorrules — Nomarc agent execution constraints

These rules are non-negotiable. They override any general habit you have as an
assistant. Read this before generating a single line of code.

## 1. Never run against production casually

- `frontend/.env` points at the **same CockroachDB cluster as production**.
- `npm run dev` **writes to live rows**. Do not "just try it" to see what a
  mutation does — read the service function instead.
- Never run `scripts/seed-*` or any `rm`/`UPDATE`/`DELETE` script without
  explicit approval — read `ls scripts/` first and assume every script there
  writes to live data.
- `lib/services/dev-reset.ts` → `resetMyAccountForTesting()` deletes the
  caller's own rows across ~20 tables. Never invoke it in dev (dev = prod DB).
  `components/dashboard/reset-account-button.tsx` is currently unimported
  dead code.
- Prefer a scratch database if you must experiment.

## 2. Verification gate — both commands, always

```bash
npm run type-check   # tsc --noEmit; necessary but NOT sufficient
npm run build        # the real verification step
```

`type-check` staying silent does **not** mean the change is safe. Three failure
classes pass `tsc` and only fail `build`:

1. A `"use server"` file exporting anything that is not an async function →
   the bundler drops **every** export in that file; callers get `undefined`.
2. Passing a component reference across the Server/Client boundary → runtime
   crash.
3. Static-vs-dynamic rendering mistakes (cookies/headers) → build error or
   stale page.

Never declare a task done on `type-check` alone. Run `npm run build`.

## 3. Architecture boundaries (do not cross)

- Data access goes through `lib/services/*` only. **Components never import
  `db` directly.**
- `"use server"` modules may export **async functions only** — no `const`, no
  types-as-values, no re-exports of non-functions.
- Shared UI lives in `components/ui/`. Anything used twice belongs there.
- Private bucket objects (`R2_PRIVATE_BUCKET`) must never be given a public
  URL. Reads only via short-lived presigned GET after an ownership check.
- Payment webhooks must be signature-verified. Never trust the request body.

## 4. Migrations are hand-applied

- `drizzle-kit generate` to write SQL; **never** `drizzle-kit push`.
- Apply one file at a time, **in order**, via
  `scripts/apply-migration.cjs`. `drizzle.config.ts` deliberately has no
  `dbCredentials` so generate cannot touch a live DB.
- Changing `lib/db/schema.ts` without adding a migration leaves the DB and the
  schema file inconsistent in ways type-checking cannot see.

## 5. Environment variable discipline

- Never commit secrets. Gitignored: `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.production`,
  `.env.local.*`, `.env.vercel*`, `.env.bak`, `.env.*.bak`. Tracked templates:
  `.env.example`, `.env.vps` — **never put a real secret in either**, because
  other suffixes (e.g. `.env.vps.local`) are *not* ignored.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is **baked at build time** and exposed to the browser —
  never a secret.
- `R2_ENDPOINT` must be the **publicly reachable** S3 endpoint. A host that
  only resolves inside Docker (`host.docker.internal`, `localhost`, `minio`)
  breaks browser uploads silently.
- Adding a required env var means updating `.env.example` and `ENV.md` in the
  same change.

## 6. No drive-by refactors

- Match the surrounding style exactly. Do not reformat untouched code.
- Do not add comments that narrate what the code already says; comment the
  *why* when it is non-obvious.
- Do not introduce a new library/dependency without stating the reason. Check
  what the repo already uses first.
- Do not delete or "clean up" features, migration files, or legacy scripts
  unless explicitly asked.

## 7. Dark mode and a11y are mandatory

- Every surface ships `dark:` variants.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for animations.
- Interactive elements keep `:focus-visible` rings; don't remove outlines.
- Inputs must be ≥16px on mobile (prevents iOS zoom).

## 8. Skeletons are co-located

- A page component and its `XxxSkeleton` export live in the same file so
  loading states cannot drift from the real layout. `loading.tsx` imports it.

## 9. Pushing

- Do not commit, push, or touch `main` unless explicitly instructed.
- Inspect `git status` / `git diff` / `git log --oneline -10` before staging.
- Stage only intended files; never stage secrets or scratch files.
